Option A: SFDX auth URL (best for headless runners)

1. On your own machine, where you're already logged in to the org, run:
sf org display --target-org fsc-qa --verbose --json
Copy the sfdxAuthUrl value. It starts with force://. If the alias isn't set up yet, run sf org login web --alias fsc-qa --instance-url https://htsw--qa.sandbox.my.salesforce.com first.
Or write it straight to a file:
sf org display --target-org fsc-qa --verbose --json | ConvertFrom-Json | % { $_.result.sfdxAuthUrl } | Set-Content auth.txt
2. Copy auth.txt to the runner. Then, as the service user, run:
sf org login sfdx-url --sfdx-url-file auth.txt --alias fsc-qa
Remove-Item auth.txt

To run as the service user, use one of these:

• Download PsExec and run psexec -u DOMAIN\svc-runner -p <password> powershell (for a local account, use .\svc-runner).
• Run runas /user:DOMAIN\svc-runner powershell. This needs an account that can log on interactively.
• For NETWORK SERVICE or SYSTEM, run psexec -u "NT AUTHORITY\NETWORK SERVICE" -i powershell, using -s for SYSTEM.

Run whoami in that window to confirm the user.
